WEBVTT


00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.940
When knitting with the ribber, sometimes
the ends stitches can be problematic.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.850
Adding extra weight with claw
weights or 7 weight hangers can help.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.770
Some machines also have
ends stitch pressure plates.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:20.840
These are the pressure plates
for a brother, KR850 for

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.460
a standard gauge machine.

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:27.265
After casting on and knitting a few
rows to get the cast on comb out of

00:00:27.265 --> 00:00:29.755
the way, drop the ribber bed slightly.

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:35.495
At the end of the main needle bed,
slip the left and the right plates

00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:41.435
over the sinker posts, and then slide
them towards the knitting position.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:44.375
The presser along the
very edge of the knitting.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.520
Raise your ribber back up and make
sure the working yarn isn't caught.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.880
Positioned properly, these little
presser plates won't interfere with

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.380
your knitting and they may help
the end stitches knit more cleanly.

